.TH DKSH 1 "2026" "dksh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dksh \- a Unix shell with a C-style scripting language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dksh
[\fB\-l\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIsource\fR | \fIscript\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dksh
is an interactive shell with pipelines, redirection, job control and tab
completion, and a scripting language with declared variables, real types,
braces, functions and classes. It does not run
.BR sh (1)
or
.BR bash (1)
syntax. It is a single static binary with no libc.
.SH OPTIONS
Short options may be combined (\fB\-nx\fR).
.TP
.BI \-c " source"
Run the string. Remaining arguments become the \fBargs\fR array.
.TP
.B \-l
Login shell: read the login profile first. Implied when argv[0] starts with a dash.
.TP
.B \-i
Interactive even if standard input is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-n
Parse and resolve only; report syntax and name errors and shadowed variables.
.TP
.B \-x
Trace: print each command to standard error as "+ cmd arg..." after expansion
and before it runs, with arguments quoted.
.TP
.B \-e, +e
Failed commands stop the script (default) / do not.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Print the syntax tree instead of running.
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Like \fB\-\-dump\-ast\fR, but drawn as an ASCII tree.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for a runtime error or failed command; 2 for a syntax or name error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dksh/profile.dksh, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dksh/profile.dksh
Login shells.
.TP
.I /etc/dksh/dkshrc.dksh, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dksh/dkshrc.dksh
Interactive shells.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/dksh/history
Command history.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dksh/lib, /usr/share/dksh/lib
Module search path for bare import names.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable syntax colors and history suggestions in the line editor (also off when TERM is dumb).
.SH SEE ALSO
The language guide, docs/language.md, and SPEC.md in the source tree.
